# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# mich: Pronoun. "(personal) inflection of ich (acc): me (direct object)"
# dich: Pronoun. "(personal) inflection of du (acc): you, thee (direct singular object)"
# ihn: Pronoun. "(personal) inflection of er (acc); him, it (masculine, direct object)."
# uns: Pronoun. "inflection of wir (acc//dat): us"
# euch: Pronoun. "accusative and dative of ihr; you, yourselves"
# hier: Adverb. "(location) here; in this place; refers to an environment one is currently in, or to something within reach"
# da: Adverb. "(local) there"
# dort: Adverb. "there, yonder"
# zurück: Adverb. "back, backward, backwards, to the rear."
mich
dich
ihn
uns
euch
hier
da
dort
zurück
